<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco cuts A-960 bunkers ex-Gulf.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts A-960 bunkers ex-Gulf.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has cut A-960 bunker fuel from Ras Tanura and Dammam by $2 a tonne to $103 a tonne ($15.81 a barrel), the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A-960 from Jeddah and Yanbu is unchanged at $105 ($16.12).</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from the Gulf is also left unchanged at $211 a tonne but increased by $1 to $217 from Jeddah and Yanbu.</p>
<p>Prices are effective February 6.</p>
</text>
